        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left scrotal swelling sensation"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Left side still feels 'bit heavy like full of water'; about the same since last visit. Onset unclear, possibly a few weeks or longer. No acute increase in size. Usually painless, with an occasional dragging heavy sensation after a long day working with tools."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated symptoms and relevant history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies dysuria, haematuria, urethral discharge, fevers, rigors, nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain. No history of sudden severe testicular pain to suggest torsion. No clear trauma recalled; reports frequently knocking himself at work."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "General examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Well appearing, no apparent distress, conversant, and a slightly vague historian."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Abdominal and inguinal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Abdomen soft and non-tender, with no masses. No palpable inguinal hernia with cough impulse."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left scrotal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Left hemiscrotum enlarged with smooth, non-erythematous, intact skin. Fluctuant, non-tender swelling superior and anterior to the testis. Left testis palpated posteriorly and feels normal in size and consistency; no discrete intratesticular solid mass. No warmth, epididymal or cord tenderness, or obvious cough impulse. Chaperone practice nurse present."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right scrotal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Right testis normal size, lie, shape, and consistency; non-tender. Epididymis and cord normal."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
